---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';

const app = 'https://github.com/albertoarena/sudo-play';
---
<Base title="Tips" description="Small ways to get more from Sudo Play: share today's pick, have a playlist ready at login, use the web player, and point the app at your own catalog.">
  <h1>Tips</h1>
  <p class="lead">Small ways to get more from Sudo Play.</p>

  <h2>Share today's pick</h2>
  <p>Everyone who chooses the same genre and mood gets the same playlist all day. Tell a teammate "rock, Debugging", and you are listening to the same thing.</p>

  <h2>Have a playlist waiting</h2>
  <p>In Settings, turn on launch at login and the daily reminder. When you start work, today's pick is ready.</p>

  <h2>Set your usual genre and mood</h2>
  <p>Settings has a default genre and mood, so the window opens on what you listen to most.</p>

  <h2>No Spotify app? Use the web player</h2>
  <p>Choose the web player in Settings, and playlists open in your browser.</p>

  <h2>Keep your hands on the keyboard</h2>
  <p>Enter plays, <kbd>N</kbd> is Next, <kbd>S</kbd> is Surprise me, and Esc closes the window. The full list is in <a href="/how-it-works/">How it works</a>.</p>

  <h2>Use your own catalog</h2>
  <p>Settings has the catalog URL. Point it at a fork, or at a private catalog of your team's playlists. That server then sees the app's daily download instead of GitHub.</p>

  <h2>Add a playlist without waiting for a release</h2>
  <p>Once your pull request is merged, your playlist reaches everyone within a day. The README explains how, in <ExternalLink href={`${app}/blob/main/README.md#adding-a-playlist`}>Adding a playlist</ExternalLink>.</p>
</Base>
